#: src/backend-settings.php:409
msgid "Use Contact Form 7 Integration"
msgstr ""

#: src/backend-settings.php:414
msgid "When enabled, the Newsman tab appears on Contact Form 7 forms in the editor (per-form list selection, email field, and properties), and submissions push the email plus marked field values to the selected Newsman list. Disable to remove all Newsman editor controls and submission handling for Contact Form 7. Note: Contact Form 7 does not store form submissions in WordPress on its own — install the companion Flamingo plugin to persist submissions and enable the API v1 subscriber export from CF7 forms."
msgstr ""

#: src/backend-settings.php:429
msgid "When enabled, the Newsman subscriber.list API v1 endpoint pulls subscribers from Flamingo Inbound Messages of the selected Contact Form 7 form instead of from WordPress users / WooCommerce orders."
msgstr ""

#: src/backend-settings.php:446
msgid "No Contact Form 7 forms are marked as newsletter forms yet. Open a CF7 form, go to the Newsman tab, and turn on both \"Send to Newsman\" and \"Newsletter form\" to make it available here."
msgstr ""

#: src/backend-settings.php:448
msgid "Only one form per store is supported. Flamingo persists every submission of the selected form to the flamingo_inbound channel matching the form slug."
msgstr ""

#: src/backend-settings.php:460
msgid "Use WPForms Integration"
msgstr ""

#: src/backend-settings.php:465
msgid "When enabled, a Newsman section appears in the Settings panel of every WPForms form (per-form list selection, email field, and properties), and submissions push the email plus marked field values to the selected Newsman list. Disable to remove all Newsman builder controls and submission handling for WPForms."
msgstr ""

#: src/backend-settings.php:485
msgid "When enabled, the Newsman subscriber.list API v1 endpoint pulls subscribers from WPForms entries of the selected form instead of from WordPress users / WooCommerce orders."
msgstr ""

#: src/backend-settings.php:487
msgid "WPForms Lite does not store form entries — only WPForms Pro persists them to the database. Without entries, this export source will return no rows. Install or upgrade to WPForms Pro to use this feature."
msgstr ""

#: src/backend-settings.php:505
msgid "No WPForms forms are marked as newsletter forms yet. Open a WPForms form, go to Settings - Newsman, and turn on both \"Send to Newsman\" and \"Newsletter form\" to make it available here."
msgstr ""

#: src/backend-settings.php:507
msgid "Only one form per store is supported. WPForms persists every submission of the selected form to wp_wpforms_entries (Pro only)."
msgstr ""

#: src/backend-settings.php:518
msgid "Use Gravity Forms Integration"
msgstr ""

#: src/backend-settings.php:523
msgid "When enabled, a \"Newsman\" sub-page appears under each form's Form Settings menu (per-form list, segment, email field, and properties), and submissions push the email plus marked field values to the selected Newsman list. Disable to remove the sub-page and stop submission forwarding for Gravity Forms."
msgstr ""

#: src/backend-settings.php:537
msgid "When enabled, the Newsman subscriber.list API v1 endpoint pulls subscribers from Gravity Forms entries of the selected form instead of from WordPress users / WooCommerce orders."
msgstr ""

#: src/backend-settings.php:554
msgid "No Gravity Forms forms are marked as newsletter forms yet. Open a Gravity Forms form, go to Form Settings - Newsman, and turn on both \"Send to Newsman\" and \"Newsletter form\" to make it available here."
msgstr ""

#: src/backend-settings.php:556
msgid "Only one form per store is supported. Gravity Forms persists every submission of the selected form to wp_gf_entry / wp_gf_entry_meta."
msgstr ""

